      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_e762fe9e",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The image shows a woman interacting with a home security system, with the text overlay 'how to keep the thefts out.' The scene depicts a common, non-toxic, practical action of securing one's home. There is no evidence of abusive, cyberbullying, harmful, hateful, misogynous, or propaganda intent. The meme's intent is to humorously or ironically suggest that the woman is taking measures to prevent theft, possibly implying that theft is a common or exaggerated concern, or that the security system is a solution to a perceived problem. The visual material (woman using security system) is mapped onto the textual material ('how to keep the thefts out') via juxtaposition, creating a light-hearted or sarcastic tone. No toxicity is present.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_6196b590"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
